## Step 6 — Buyer Spec Audit

### Phase 1 — Top 2 RFQ Specs

Provided buyer specs: Toilet Seat Type (Indian / Western), Length (3–6 ft), Width (3–6 ft).

**Toilet Seat Type** (Indian / Western):
- Non-interchangeable requirement. A seller supplying only Indian-style pans cannot fulfil a Western-style requirement. This is the single most important routing signal — it immediately eliminates half the seller pool.
- **Rank 1.**

**Length** (3 / 3.5 / 4 / 5 / 6 ft):
- Cabin footprint determines whether the unit fits the available site space. Sellers need this to confirm they can supply the required size. Also drives price (larger cabin = higher price).
- **Rank 2.**

*(Width carries similar information to Length — together they define footprint. But Length is the primary dimension buyers specify first. Width is redundant once Length is known for standard cabin proportions. Length is the better single representative.)*

### Phase 2 — Thumbnail Eligibility

**Toilet Seat Type** (Indian / Western):
- Indian squat pan vs Western commode are visually distinct product types. A buyer scanning thumbnails can immediately identify which style is shown.
- **Thumbnail eligible: true.** Options: ["Indian", "Western"]

**Length** (3 ft / 3.5 ft / 4 ft / 5 ft / 6 ft):
- Dimensional spec — no meaningful visual difference between a 3 ft and 4 ft cabin in a thumbnail image.
- **Thumbnail eligible: false.**

